    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T14:23:16Z",
    "body": "Maintainer decision, 2026-11-22, given in the question dialog: **accepted**.\n\nA wave of PRs that the planner groups together gets ONE heavy run on a trial tree of the wave (current `main` plus each PR of the wave). The result is recorded on each PR of the wave (tree hash, lanes, counts). A red step is attributed to a PR, that PR leaves the wave, and the run starts again for the rest.\n\nRules that stay:\n- \"Not run\" is never a pass.\n- A PR that merges alone keeps the rule of today.\n- The release tier at the cut stays the final check.\n\nNext step: a process PR (`Process change: yes`) with the decision entry in `docs/decisions/`, the text of AGENTS.md (\"Heavy lanes at review\"), the `gate`, `merge-ready` and `review-prs` skills, and `cargo xtask gate heavy` accepting a trial tree and printing the PR heads that it covers. Safety-floor PRs: the wave run covers them only if the trial tree contains their final head.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
